//! Project: tide-chart (cli)
//! AC description: `tide-chart chart --today --root <dir>` reads `<dir>/tide.db` and prints a 4-line ASCII chart for the last 24 hours to stdout: one line per signal, each line 24 columns wide, using one of `▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█` or `.+*#` characters to encode normalized intensity. Each line is prefixed with the signal name (8 chars, left-padded). Exits 0 on success.
//! Test predicate: tests/acceptance_ac2.rs
//!
//! Ownership split: this //! header block (AC metadata) is
//! read-only — to change an AC, file
//! agent/intent_card_amendment_request.json and re-scaffold. The
//! `fn acceptance_ac2` body BELOW is owned by the edit-agent: replace
//! the panic stub with a real assertion that verifies the AC
